Bicep Template Parameters:
Parameter name must be unique and not shared with variables, resources, etc.
param storageAccountName string = 'myStorageAccount'
param storageAccountCount int = 2
param location string = resourceGroup().location

'storageAccountName' builds a dynamic parameter using the parameter named 'environment'. 
param environment string = 'dev'
param storageAccountName string = 'sa${environment}01'


Bicep Template Resources:

param storageAccountName string = 'myStorageAccount'
param location string = 'westus2'

resource storageAccount 'Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts@2024-01-01' = {
  name: storageAccountName
  location: location
  sku: {
    name: 'Standard_LRS'
  }
kind: 'StorageV2'
  properties: {
    accessTier: 'Hot'
    supportsHttpsTrafficOnly: 'true'
  }
 }

Bicep templates can be both reusable and expressive by using decorator @description and @metadata.
During deployment, the template will prompt user for an environment name. If no name is added for  
the environment name then 'dev' will be added as default.
@description: 'The deployment environment (e.g. dev, test, prod).'
@metadata({
  businessUnit: 'Finance'
  contact: 'Data Admins'
})
@allowed ([
  'dev'
  'test'
  'prod'
])
param environment string = 'dev'
